1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,920
It’s difficult not to admire the talent of a skilled musician.
很难不钦佩技艺精湛的音乐家的才华。

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:14,660
Whether it be a pianist, flautist or cellist, these individuals have shown dedication and passion over a long period of time to reach the highest levels of performance.
无论是钢琴家、长笛演奏家还是大提琴演奏家，这些人都凭借长期的付出与热爱，才达到了顶尖的演奏水准。

3
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:18,600
But they say it’s never too late to learn.
但人们常说，学习永远不嫌晚。

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:24,880
So what are the benefits, for both children and adults, in learning a musical instrument?
那么，学习一门乐器对儿童和成人而言，究竟有哪些益处呢？

5
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:31,100
Learning to play a musical instrument when growing up can improve hearing in adulthood.
年少时学习演奏乐器，有助于提升成年后的听力水平。

6
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:44,490
According to a study by Dr Nina Kraus, Professor of Neurobiology at Northwestern University in Illinois, US, children who played musical instruments were better at recognising different frequencies.
美国伊利诺伊州西北大学神经生物学教授妮娜·克劳斯博士的一项研究表明，学过乐器的儿童更善于分辨不同的音频。

7
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:54,660
This improved hearing skill carried over into later life with adults who had once played an instrument able to discern sounds of different pitches more easily.
这种提升后的听力技能会延续到日后的生活中，曾学过乐器的成年人能更轻松地辨别不同音高的声音。

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:57,980
And it could also have some academic benefits too.
此外，学习乐器对学业也有帮助。

9
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:11,300
A study conducted by the University of British Columbia found that students who engaged in music-related activities during grades 7-12 scored significantly higher in science, English and maths.
英属哥伦比亚大学的一项研究发现，在7至12年级期间参与过音乐相关活动的学生，在科学、英语和数学学科的成绩要显著更高。

10
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:13,930
And there are not just benefits to children.
学习乐器的益处并非只针对儿童。

11
00:01:13,930 --> 00:01:21,560
Whether you choose to play the piano, pick or strum a guitar or learn a drumbeat, you could end up joining a band or orchestra.
无论你选择弹钢琴、拨弄吉他、扫弦，还是学习打鼓，最终都有可能加入一支乐队或管弦乐团。

12
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:29,110
This in turn could improve your social life, meeting other bandmates who are likeminded in their love of a good tune.
这进而能丰富你的社交生活，结识其他志同道合、同样热爱美妙旋律的乐队伙伴。

13
00:01:29,110 --> 00:01:33,220
Learning an instrument can also give you a sense of achievement.
学习乐器还能带给你成就感。

14
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:42,590
Nailing that perfect chord is one way, but what if you got together with a bunch of friends and entered into a battle of the bands – and won?
弹出一组完美的和弦是一种成就，但如果你和一群朋友组队参加乐队大赛并夺冠，那种成就感又会是怎样的呢？

15
00:01:42,590 --> 00:01:49,840
So, whether you’re looking to destress playing out some chords, or improve your grades at school, maybe taking up an instrument could help you.
所以，无论你是想通过弹奏和弦来减压，还是希望提高学业成绩，或许学习一门乐器都能帮到你。
